>
  <h2>Profile</h2>
  <p>
    Born in 1990, Osaka, Japan.
    Founder of the family-oriented gift brand <strong>"Selfeliz,"</strong>
    overseeing design, product development, and brand strategy.
    She develops products with a strong focus on functionality, comfort for sensitive skin,
    and the quality of <strong>unseen processes</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Blending European aesthetics with Japanese quality standards, she positions Selfeliz as
    a brand that <strong>"designs family relationships and time."</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>Current Activities</h2>
  <p>
    Founder of the family-oriented gift brand "Selfeliz," overseeing the entire process from
    concept and design to product development and sales strategy.
    She focuses on developing products that prioritize functionality and comfort,
    particularly for sensitive skin, while expanding both domestically and internationally
    through pop-ups, exhibitions, and collaborations.
  </p>

  <h2>Background &amp; Origin</h2>
  <p>
    Her journey began with her child's atopic condition, which led her to study nutrition
    and develop a deeper awareness of what we bring into our bodies.
    This awareness naturally extended to clothing, leading her to launch a European
    children's wear selection business in 2023, followed by the creation of her original
    brand, Selfeliz, in 2024.
  </p>

  <h2>Career</h2>
  <p>
    Through her experience in a garment factory handling inspection and quality
    control, she developed the belief that <strong>"the true value of a product lies in
    the unseen processes."</strong>
    She later worked as a nail artist for six years, focusing on structural design and
    functionality. After marriage and raising four children, she gained further experience
    supporting business operations, forming the foundation of her current brand management.
  </p>

  <h2>Production &amp; Quality Control</h2>
  <p>
    She partners with manufacturing factories in China that have experience working with
    Japanese companies, ensuring high standards of quality and communication.
    In 2026, she visited the factory to oversee production processes and develop new products.
    She places strong emphasis on direct engagement with production teams, even in an
    increasingly digital business environment.
  </p>

  <h2>Brand Concept</h2>
  <p>
    Selfeliz is not simply a children's brand, but a brand that <strong>"designs family
    relationships and time."</strong>
    It integrates thoughtful material selection, structural design, and comfort to deliver
    products that ensure both aesthetic and functional reliability.
  </p>

  <h2>Philosophy &amp; Message</h2>
  <p>
    Her philosophy centers on delivering not just products, but meaningful experiences and
    relationships. Through everyday choices, she aims to support families in creating a more
    comfortable and fulfilling life.
  </p>
</PartnerLayout>
